import json,hashlib,re,datetime,subprocess
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];ids=json.loads((p/'reservation.json').read_text())['ids'];prov=json.loads((p/'provenance.json').read_text()); inv=json.loads((p/'sources/version-inventory.json').read_text())
notes={
322013:('parked_no_full_route','v2 Conjecture 12.8; v3 Conjecture 13.8 and preceding fixed-space definitions; v1 introduction; author PDF Quillen-fiber definition and cone lemma','Tried the common-vertex criterion on fixed-space fibers. A cone vertex must belong to every maximal face of the fiber, not merely make its order complex contractible. The source already treats Coxeter and Shephard systems. A bad fiber for one generating set cannot refute the existential quantifier on R.','Need either a new uniform choice of R for the remaining groups or a specific W with a proof that every rank-sized reflection generating set fails. Neither exists here; no finite obstruction supplied.'),
322517:('parked_infinite_degree_spectrum','v1 Conjecture 5.8','Norm-one diagonalization would have to defeat all computable copies H and all one-query reductions simultaneously. Merely encoding a chosen function by attaching graph gadgets proves no avoidance property.','Need a computable approximation with at most n downward changes per input, plus diagonal requirements uniformly across all copies; no priority construction supplied. Literal record contains corrupted reduction notation.'),
319799:('parked_uniform_extremal','v1/v2 introduction; v2 Conjecture 1.10, Corollary 1.9, geometric-copy definition','A single finite dense geometric graph cannot contradict existence of c_k. Taking F complete recovers the pairwise crossing extremal subproblem. Source matching means disjoint endpoints with prescribed crossings, not arbitrary edge copies.','Need an unbounded-density F-avoiding family for one fixed circle graph, or a full uniform linear bound. Neither route available.'),
320610:('parked_infinite_classification','v1/v2/v3 Conjecture 6.1; v3 known k<=3 scope','Hitting unsatisfiability gives a partition of the Boolean cube into clause-falsifying subcubes. The identity sum_C 2^(-|C|)=1 does not bound variables at fixed deficiency. Non-singularity rules out the simplest repeatedly split-clause construction.','Need an explicit fixed-deficiency infinite non-singular family, or a bound on n(F) in terms of c(F)-n(F). No such bound/construction proved.'),
320804:('parked_uniform_ramsey','v1 Conjecture B and product/group-action equivalences','Hales-Jewett supplies a monochromatic combinatorial line but its number of moving coordinates depends on the colouring. Turning that into the required congruent unscaled X forces a scaling choice with the wrong quantifier order.','Need predetermined scale and n for every colouring, not scale selected after seeing a monochromatic line. Source equivalences alone are no new proof.'),
320805:('parked_uniform_ramsey','v1 Conjecture D, block definition, Proposition 2.2','Ordinary Hales-Jewett drops the fixed positive degree d; that weakening is explicitly proved in the source. Empty individual blocks are allowed, but all blocks empty would have degree zero and cannot solve the assertion.','Need d selected before the colouring and guaranteed positive. No colour-independent block-degree mechanism.'),
320911:('parked_analytic_uniform','v1 Conjecture 4.1 and following two-dimensional comparison','Affine ellipsoid/transplantation bounds address source special families. They do not compare all convex bodies, all dimensions and all partial Neumann sums. Translating the origin also changes the polar body.','Need rigorous spectral inequalities for general convex domains; no exact analytic witness or universal comparison produced.'),
318150:('parked_infinite_number_theory','v1/v2/v3 conjecture/status passages; latest inspected text includes unrelated Pell counterexamples','A finite modular obstruction might refute one representation clause, but Fibonacci/Lucas parity alone leaves admissible residues. Printed counterexamples to Pell variants concern different sequences and coefficients.','No covering congruence or exact unrepresentable integer for the stated Lucas/Fibonacci clauses. No uniform prime-representation proof.'),
318395:('excluded_published_resolution','v1/v2 Conjecture 5 and Proposition 8; Fischer 0907.0401 Theorem 1 and Section 6 equation (6.1); 1008.0527 coefficient discussion','Complete published reduction: Fischer Theorem 1 identifies the binomial-basis coefficients with the monotone-trapezoid counts at increasing indices. Reflect/translate the bottom row of alpha(n;k_1,...,k_n), then change binomial bases. Section 6 gives exactly the reversed-index signed product-binomial relation (6.1) for all indices, explicitly identifying it as Fischer-Romik Conjecture 5. Coefficients provide the extension.','No discovery credit: exact general linear-equations conjecture is publicly proved. Uniqueness conjectures are different questions, not this reservation.'),
317029:('parked_exact_permutation_counts','v1 definitions, Conjecture 1, divisibility discussion; Kral-Pikhurko journal Theorem 3 and proof opening','Tried inversion/pattern moment constraints and finite-to-limit rigidity. Uniform k-pattern counts imply lower pattern uniformity by double-counting extensions. This supplies the printed divisibility restrictions, not sufficiency. Theorem 3 for permutons uses independent samples: repeated selection of a finite permutation cell introduces collision terms, so finite exact 4-symmetry does not give a 4-symmetric permuton.','Need a finite identity forcing a contradiction at an admissible n (e.g. n=64,k=4), or a full construction for every admissible pair. No identity/witness. The record status quotation concerns Graham asymptotic questions, not Conjecture 1.'),
317510:('parked_universal_partial_fields','v2 Section 6 definition of level partial fields, Conjecture 6.6; v1 target text not located','The word level does not make the required homomorphism tautological: the class used to build the level field and the class of all its represented matroids require comparison. Counting homomorphisms to GF(5) does not construct one to every eligible target partial field.','Need the universal property with exact lift/class definitions. Hydra-k omissions are explicitly noted by source. No construction or obstruction.'),
317936:('parked_bound_gap','v1 Conjecture 4.4; v2 Conjecture 4.5, Theorems 4.7,5.5, Proposition 5.4','Characteristic zero is proved by source. Theorem 5.5 proves positive characteristic above U(w), whereas the literal asks above N(w). Substituting U for N changes scope.','Need compare U(w) and N(w), or control Lefschetz data for every characteristic in the gap. No such proof, and no current claim of resolution.'),
316289:('parked_graph_angle_system','v1/v2 Section 13 conjectures and constraining definition; Ringel status paragraph','Source refutation quotation refers to Ringel slope conjecture, not the constraining conjecture 13.15. Cubic directed cases already appear in source; recycling their angle determinant gives no full general proof.','Need an order/constraint/compatible-angle construction for every minimal simply three-edge-connected totally cyclic digraph, with strict infeasibility and nonzero homogeneous kernel. No full construction.'),
379793:('parked_representation_bridge','v1/v2 Conjecture B; v2 Section 5.1 examples and 5.2 reciprocity discussion','q inversion plus Hecke sign twist is a plausible route, but it must identify the cyclic generators and lambda-to-transpose decomposition including singular specialization. Source already gives n=2,3 multiplicities and extreme partitions; formula evaluation in these ranges is not new.','Need a generator-preserving intertwiner for all n or a genuine singular rank mismatch outside printed formulas. No such bridge or witness.'),
379797:('parked_uniform_orthogonality','v1/v2 Conjecture 11.2, source dimension reduction; latest version checked ranks<=7','Equal dimensions reduce equality to pairwise orthogonality phi_c^-1(alpha_i) perpendicular beta_j, exactly as source prints. Coxeter-element rotation needs compatibility of the recursively transformed lower/upper labels, not just preservation of root inner products.','Need a rotation/mutation lemma proving that compatibility for arbitrary c and all clusters, or a rank>7 exact failure. Neither supplied. Checked ranges cannot receive credit.'),
379977:('parked_infinite_word_classification','v1/v2 Conjecture 13, construction and adjacent Theorem 14','A finite non-paperfolding word is insufficient: must extend infinitely while avoiding squares at every odd difference, and fail membership in every relevant orbit closure. Literal alphabet relabeling gives only a convention correction, excluded.','Need an infinite extension theorem for a forbidden prefix, or full classification. No automatic word with a proved avoidance/orbit obstruction.'),
379982:('excluded_printed_counterexamples','v1 Conjecture 1, Facts 1-3, Figure 1 discussion, Theorem 2.1 and proof cases; later 0906.0895 abstract','Source explicitly supplies order-11 G1,G2 with delta=3, 2-connectivity, induced-K1,5-freeness and 3-vertex-criticality but no perfect matching after the indicated deletion. Theorem 2.1 classifies them as the only exceptions; the proof case k=5 refers back to the printed graphs.','Already refuted in its cited source. Figures not visually transcribed in this lane, so no independently reconstructed adjacency certificate claimed; textual primary exclusion is decisive.'),
378963:('parked_asymptotic_structure','v1 Theorem 1.4, Examples 1.2,1.5,1.6 and surrounding conjecture discussion','Three separated equal intervals approach doubling 10/3 and are explicitly printed. Their ratio tends to 10/3, so for any fixed alpha<10/3 they eventually fail the hypothesis and cannot refute the existence of K. Small finite exceptions also do not refute an eventual statement.','Need an unbounded family with one fixed alpha<10/3 avoiding both prescribed progression covers. Source proves only a small-epsilon interval; no extension to entire interval.'),
379094:('parked_after_sustained_finite_attempt','v1 Definitions 1-6, Theorems 12-14 with proofs, Conjecture 24 and cover-pebbling comparison','Tried concentration via a lexicographically maximal unsolvable configuration, root-distance potentials, and multiple demand bottlenecks. Moving a price packet consumes p_i-1 pebbles, so legal moves cannot be used to preserve the extremal total while concentrating. Fixed-target potentials certify unsolvability but do not prove all configurations of k pebbles solvable. Source complete/path/star formulas already realize its concentration recipes.','Need one explicit graph/price/t and an unsolvable lower-bound configuration exceeding every conjectured-shape obstruction, together with proofs every shape at that size is t-solvable, or a mass-preserving concentration lemma. No graph or qualified finite witness furnished; generic reachability enumeration is not a candidate.'),
379147:('excluded_source_refutation','Kozlov v1 Sections 3.1,3.2,3.5; Proposition 3.5.4 and printed Counterexample/Figure 3.4','Published counterexample uses n=23, lambda=(7,6,4,3,2,1), mu=(10,8,5). Proposition 3.5.4 identifies connected components of X_lambda,mu and its marked-partition poset. Figure 3.4 gives two components; the Sundaram-Welker homology decomposition translates this non-acyclic summand to failure of the vanishing claim.','No credit: counterexample explicitly in cited text. Full homology-bridge formalization and figure reconstruction not undertaken; no new numerical homology assertion.')}
